      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, so i added s3:ListBucket and s3:GetBucketLocation to the policy for the bucket ARN (not just the /* path) and it still isn't working. i'm still getting that same access denied error. \n\nit feels like something is just blocking it from getting in. is there any other way something could be interfering with the access, like maybe a setting on the bucket itself or something else in aws that could be acting as a gatekeeper?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most likely remaining issue is an S3 Bucket Policy explicitly denying access or restricting it to IPv4 clients, which you are not using. Additionally, if you are using `cloudwatch:PutLogEvents` on the service itself, the IAM principal must have `s3:ListBucket` on that specific bucket to even understand it exists. However, since you've done that, check if your Lambda execution policy has a condition requiring specific source IPs; if so, remove the `aws:SourceIp` condition temporarily to test. Finally, ensure you are using `arn:aws:s3:::my-company-log-bucket` for the ListBucket action and not `arn:aws:s3:::my-company-log-bucket/*` in the same statement if needed.",
